# Variadic param collects excess positional args only — not named args.
# Named args can target regular params by name; the variadic only receives positional overflow.
# Calling with a named arg for x (no excess positional) produces an empty variadic dict.
[f: [fn [let x ...rest] rest]
 result: [f x: 42]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x, rest), "result": Dict({})})
